#: app/data/werner.profile.ts#getWernerProfileCopy
msgid ""
"# Sebastian Werner\n"
"\n"
"**Principal Technology Consultant · Detailed Project Profile**\n"
"\n"
"I build frontend architectures for new software products and modernize "
"existing platforms. Internationalization, UI quality, performance, and "
"developer tooling are recurring responsibilities. My experience covers "
"enterprise software, banking, energy, commerce, telecommunications, and "
"industrial applications.\n"
"\n"
"## Project experience\n"
"\n"
"### 3Degrees · Meridian\n"
"\n"
"**November 2025–present · Senior Principal Frontend Architect · US-client "
"engagement**\n"
"\n"
"I lead work on visual quality, internationalization, and frontend performance "
"for an energy-management product. My work includes marketplace and public "
"product pages, mobile layouts, SEO, and separate rendering paths for public "
"pages and authenticated portals.\n"
"\n"
"I introduced application localization and migrated the runtime from Lingui to "
"Palamedes, including per-request language handling and translation-catalog "
"boundaries between server and client code. Performance work covers "
"language-specific HTML and data caching, reduced client-side work, and "
"progressive streaming of portfolio information. The team works entirely in "
"English and uses AI-supported development extensively.\n"
"\n"
"**Relevant technologies:** TypeScript, React, Next.js, Palamedes, Lingui, "
"Vercel, Cloudflare, Supabase.\n"
"\n"
"### Regrello\n"
"\n"
"**October 2024–September 2025 · Frontend Internationalization Lead · "
"US-client engagement**\n"
"\n"
"I led the internationalization of an established enterprise application. I "
"integrated localization into the UI and built catalog extraction, compilation,"
" and LLM-assisted translation workflows. These workflows retained translation "
"metadata and language-specific terminology.\n"
"\n"
"As part of a shared initiative, I implemented review interfaces for translated"
" user content. They covered rich text, mention placeholders, "
"permission-sensitive editing, and asynchronous states.\n"
"\n"
"I also migrated the frontend workspace from NX to Turborepo, introduced strict"
" type-aware linting, and automated GraphQL enum-to-union migration. I "
"separated component-development dependencies from the main application and "
"added targeted UI and end-to-end tests.\n"
"\n"
"**Relevant technologies:** TypeScript, React, GraphQL, Lingui, Vite, "
"Turborepo, Storybook, Playwright.\n"
"\n"
"### EnBW · Customer Portals and Support Workbench\n"
"\n"
"**June 2022–February 2024 · Frontend Expert / React Architect**\n"
"\n"
"I contributed frontend architecture and implementation to customer "
"self-service and support applications. The white-label platform supported "
"tenant-specific features, content, communication options, and visual identity."
" Customer workflows included contracts, invoices, meter readings, tariff "
"changes, and relocation.\n"
"\n"
"I built the PNPM/Turborepo workspace, shared theme and configuration packages,"
" Storybook foundations, typed API integration, and reusable data-access "
"utilities. I documented how to separate routing and data integration from "
"reusable, API-independent presentation layouts. The architecture used headless"
" UI primitives and typed style/asset themes.\n"
"\n"
"**Relevant technologies:** React, TypeScript, PNPM, Turborepo, Vite, "
"Storybook, Radix, VanillaExtract, SWR, REST, GraphQL.\n"
"\n"
"### Azeti · Industrial Monitoring Platform\n"
"\n"
"**March–May 2022 · Senior React Developer**\n"
"\n"
"I helped develop an industrial monitoring product with a white-label frontend."
" My work covered the NX monorepo, internationalization, theming options, and "
"application components.\n"
"\n"
"**Relevant technologies:** React, NX, internationalization, theming.\n"
"\n"
"### Netze BW · Customer Portal\n"
"\n"
"**February 2021–February 2022 · Lead Web Frontend Architect**\n"
"\n"
"I worked on architecture and development of a customer portal for master data "
"and photovoltaic-installation management. I combined API-first development "
"with architectural improvements, feature design, and Cypress-based end-to-end "
"tests. The team included external specialists, CGI consultants, and internal "
"project and UX staff.\n"
"\n"
"**Relevant technologies:** React, REST, Cypress, API-first development, "
"Scrum.\n"
"\n"
"### empiriecom · Otto Group\n"
"\n"
"**November 2020–February 2021 · Frontend / GraphQL Development Support**\n"
"\n"
"I supported GraphQL and frontend development within the Otto Group. I worked "
"on resolvers, database integration, typing and testability, and a shared "
"component library. I also helped identify conceptual gaps and clarify "
"implementation questions.\n"
"\n"
"**Relevant technologies:** GraphQL, Apollo, TypeScript, Node.js, MySQL.\n"
"\n"
"### HeidelbergCement / Heidelberg Materials\n"
"\n"
"**June 2019–September 2020 · React Architect**\n"
"\n"
"I developed and modernized web applications, including a truck-tracking "
"interface with a heuristic for route visualization. My work included a shared "
"frontend monorepo, Azure/CDN deployment tooling, TypeScript migration, "
"API-client improvements, and Cypress tests. I worked with UX designers on "
"reusable React interface foundations.\n"
"\n"
"**Relevant technologies:** React, TypeScript, Google Maps, Azure, CDN, "
"Cypress, Axios.\n"
"\n"
"### GE Healthcare\n"
"\n"
"**February 2019 · React Training and Mentoring**\n"
"\n"
"I delivered a workshop on React architecture, project structure, assets, "
"TypeScript, server-data interaction, Redux conventions, and GraphQL. The "
"workshop focused on applying these concepts to frontend design and "
"implementation.\n"
"\n"
"**Relevant technologies:** React, TypeScript, Redux, GraphQL.\n"
"\n"
"### Witt · Otto Group\n"
"\n"
"**September 2018–June 2019 · React / GraphQL Architect**\n"
"\n"
"I worked on a multilingual, multi-brand commerce platform with product pages, "
"a basket, and customer accounts, including internationalization for Eastern "
"European markets. On my initiative, we introduced GraphQL to orchestrate "
"multiple backend services and give the frontend a consistent API.\n"
"\n"
"I worked on server-rendered shop pages, incremental client loading through "
"code splitting, efficient bundles, and Webpack/build tooling. The development "
"workflow included performance monitoring. I also worked on routing and "
"preloading, SSR-compatible user handling, and developer mentoring.\n"
"\n"
"**Relevant technologies:** React, Apollo/GraphQL, SSR, Webpack, Babel, code "
"splitting.\n"
"\n"
"### SWR · ARD Mediathek\n"
"\n"
"**July–September 2018 · React / GraphQL Development**\n"
"\n"
"I contributed to the shared ARD media-library frontend for HbbTV televisions "
"and desktop, tablet, and mobile browsers. I integrated GraphQL over existing "
"REST APIs and implemented frontend features under constrained-device "
"performance requirements.\n"
"\n"
"**Relevant technologies:** React, GraphQL, REST, HbbTV, responsive "
"interfaces.\n"
"\n"
"### INIT · Public-Transport Information Dashboard\n"
"\n"
"**April–July 2018 · React Architect**\n"
"\n"
"I worked with product and development leadership on the architecture and "
"implementation of a real-time transport-information dashboard. My contribution"
" included API orchestration, geographic data presentation, reusable interface "
"components, and React knowledge transfer.\n"
"\n"
"**Relevant technologies:** React, Apollo/GraphQL, REST, Mapbox, "
"OpenStreetMap.\n"
"\n"
"### Traton · RIO\n"
"\n"
"**January–March 2018 · Senior React Developer**\n"
"\n"
"I helped develop an existing telematics platform for logistics companies in a "
"distributed team. I contributed application code, architecture suggestions, "
"and mentoring.\n"
"\n"
"**Relevant technologies:** React, Redux, Webpack.\n"
"\n"
"### coliquio\n"
"\n"
"**June–December 2017 · React / Frontend Architect**\n"
"\n"
"I worked on a new application connecting pharmaceutical representatives and "
"physicians. I restructured a component library and contributed responsive "
"layouts, typography, server rendering, and code splitting. I also evaluated "
"interface components, advised on architecture, and trained developers.\n"
"\n"
"**Relevant technologies:** React, SSR, CSS Grid, Webpack, component "
"libraries.\n"
"\n"
"### Deutsche Bank · BluePort Corporate Banking\n"
"\n"
"**2017 · Frontend Architect**\n"
"\n"
"I contributed frontend architecture and technology decisions for a "
"corporate-banking platform. I worked on technical guidance, reviewed code for "
"two offshore development teams, and helped plan their development "
"environment.\n"
"\n"
"**Relevant technologies and methods:** React, Git-based review workflows, "
"SAFe/Scaled Agile, distributed-team enablement.\n"
"\n"
"### Berlitz · Language-Course Portal\n"
"\n"
"**2016–2017 · React / Frontend Architect**\n"
"\n"
"I worked on a portal for planning and delivering language courses. I "
"simplified frontend architecture and tooling, contributed GraphQL/Apollo "
"integration, and supported implementation and the development team.\n"
"\n"
"**Relevant technologies:** React, Apollo/GraphQL, Webpack.\n"
"\n"
"### DIY Retailer · Online Shop\n"
"\n"
"**2016 · React Development and Architecture Support**\n"
"\n"
"I developed the shop frontend and its tooling, including PostCSS, React "
"hot-module replacement alongside server rendering, and internationalization. I"
" also worked on separate application output for desktop and mobile "
"interfaces.\n"
"\n"
"**Relevant technologies:** React, React Intl, SSR/HMR, PostCSS, Webpack.\n"
"\n"
"### Cleverbridge · Customer Portal\n"
"\n"
"**April–May 2016 · React Development**\n"
"\n"
"I supported AOE in evaluating Vue and React, then contributed to the React "
"implementation of Cleverbridge's customer portal.\n"
"\n"
"**Relevant technologies:** React, Vue evaluation.\n"
"\n"
"### Deutsche Asset & Wealth Management / Deutsche Bank · Robo-Advisor\n"
"\n"
"**2015–2016 · Lead Frontend Architecture and Development**\n"
"\n"
"I worked with a small specialist team on an investment application. I built "
"frontend foundations and interactive charts showing portfolio value and "
"potential development, selecting Vue for the interface and D3 for "
"visualization. The project followed formal requirements, approval procedures, "
"and release processes.\n"
"\n"
"**Relevant technologies:** Vue, D3, Sass, JavaScript.\n"
"\n"
"### Huawei / Deutsche Telekom · EntertainTV\n"
"\n"
"**June 2014–October 2015 · Frontend / UI Architect**\n"
"\n"
"I worked on the interface for a new generation of Telekom set-top boxes. The "
"hardware required careful performance work to deliver demanding visual design,"
" animation, and interaction.\n"
"\n"
"I implemented animations, layouts, and the electronic program guide, tuned UI "
"performance, and coordinated with on-site and offshore developers and design "
"stakeholders.\n"
"\n"
"**Relevant technologies:** JavaScript, Velocity.js, UI animation, "
"constrained-device performance, frontend tooling.\n"
"\n"
"### MAGIX and TeleColumbus · Triplesense Reply\n"
"\n"
"**2013–2014 · Frontend Development**\n"
"\n"
"I worked on a responsive MAGIX website and a mobile TeleColumbus product/order"
" application. For MAGIX, I developed viewport-based typography, interface "
"behavior, and product-finder/comparison features. For TeleColumbus, I worked "
"on client-side navigation, templated interfaces, form feedback, and PHP/RPC "
"integration.\n"
"\n"
"**Relevant technologies:** JavaScript, HTML/CSS, Sass, Jasy, RPC.\n"
"\n"
"### Deutsche Telekom · Telefoniecenter\n"
"\n"
"**November 2012–April 2013 · Frontend Development and Architecture**\n"
"\n"
"I built frontend functionality for fixed-line telephony configuration, "
"including call forwarding, blocked callers, and tariff options. The "
"implementation used MVP-style templates, REST integration, live validation, "
"and background synchronization, with Core and Jasy infrastructure.\n"
"\n"
"**Relevant technologies:** JavaScript, HTML5, REST, Core, Jasy.\n"
"\n"
"### Zynga\n"
"\n"
"**April 2011–November 2012 · Senior JavaScript Developer**\n"
"\n"
"I worked on HTML5 game infrastructure, UI performance, and developer tooling "
"in a large JavaScript environment. Core and Jasy were developed on our own "
"initiative and used extensively at Zynga: Core as the base library for our "
"games and Jasy for their build process.\n"
"\n"
"Both were developed further during the engagement, including framework, "
"compiler/build, translation, asset, and development-server capabilities. My "
"scrolling and animation work addressed the runtime demands of large game "
"interfaces.\n"
"\n"
"**Relevant technologies:** JavaScript, HTML5, Python, Core, Jasy, performance "
"tooling.\n"
"\n"
"### Deutsche Telekom · Unify and Early Tolino Software\n"
"\n"
"**2009–2011 · Frontend Architecture and Development**\n"
"\n"
"I contributed to Unify, Deutsche Telekom's open-source framework, and worked "
"on a soccer app built with PhoneGap and Unify. I also developed early Tolino "
"software for desktop browsers, using qooxdoo, rich animations, and efficient "
"ePub rendering.\n"
"\n"
"**Relevant technologies:** JavaScript, qooxdoo, Unify, PhoneGap, ePub, UI "
"animation.\n"
"\n"
"### studiVZ\n"
"\n"
"**October 2008–February 2009 · JavaScript Team Lead**\n"
"\n"
"I led a team of four frontend specialists working on a rapidly grown codebase."
" I developed interface components, including a photo viewer with person "
"tagging.\n"
"\n"
"**Relevant technologies:** JavaScript, interface architecture, team "
"leadership.\n"
"\n"
"### 1&1 · qooxdoo\n"
"\n"
"**November 2004–September 2008 · Lead Developer**\n"
"\n"
"I led development of the qooxdoo JavaScript UI framework. My work covered "
"component and property systems, widgets, layout and rendering infrastructure, "
"internationalization, and keyboard and focus behavior. I also worked on "
"Python-based JavaScript compilation/build tooling, the open-source community, "
"and technical presentations.\n"
"\n"
"**Relevant technologies:** JavaScript, Python, UI frameworks, compiler/build "
"systems, internationalization.\n"
"\n"
"### Schlund+Partner / 1&1\n"
"\n"
"**May 2002–October 2004 · Web Developer**\n"
"\n"
"In my first employed development role, I worked on recursive XSLT/Pustefix "
"templates for products and ordering. I also developed client-side "
"JavaScript/CSS interactions and worked on the DSL storefront, Control Center, "
"and newsletters.\n"
"\n"
"**Relevant technologies:** XSLT, Pustefix, JavaScript, CSS.\n"
"\n"
"## Selected open-source work\n"
"\n"
"Open source is part of my engineering practice and a way to give back to the "
"developer community. These projects make the work available for other "
"developers to use, review, and build on.\n"
"\n"
"| Project | Contribution and relevance |\n"
"| --- | --- |\n"
"| [Palamedes](https://github.com/sebastian-software/palamedes) / "
"[Ferrocat](https://github.com/sebastian-software/ferrocat) | "
"Internationalization, translation-catalog processing and workflows, Rust "
"architecture, typed Node.js interfaces, and framework integration. |\n"
"| [Ferroni](https://github.com/sebastian-software/ferroni) / "
"[Ferriki](https://github.com/sebastian-software/ferriki) | Ports and "
"modernization of existing regex/tokenization foundations, compatibility "
"checks, Rust performance work, and native JavaScript integration. |\n"
"| [Ferralk](https://github.com/sebastian-software/ferralk) | File discovery, "
"matching, and parallel traversal in Rust, with work on ownership, allocation, "
"and performance-regression checks. |\n"
"| [Ferromark](https://github.com/sebastian-software/ferromark) | "
"Markdown/document tooling, native interfaces, and performance optimization of "
"existing open-source code, retaining upstream attribution. |\n"
"| [Dalo](https://github.com/sebastian-software/dalo) | Rust CLI for versioned "
"agent skills, source synchronization, ownership, and actionable diagnostics. "
"|\n"
"| [Naos UI](https://github.com/sebastian-software/naos-ui) | UI compiler with "
"TypeScript, native Node.js, and WASM integration. |\n"
"| [Ardo](https://github.com/sebastian-software/ardo) | React documentation "
"infrastructure, reusable UI foundations, typed content, and API documentation."
" |\n"
"| [Effective Agent](https://github.com/sebastian-software/effective-agent) | "
"Engineering guidance for coding agents, with intent routing, maintained "
"references, and validation. |\n"
"| [Effective Icon](https://github.com/sebastian-software/effective-icon) | "
"Build-time UI tooling that resolves named icons to the assets actually used. "
"|\n"
"| [Impeccino](https://github.com/sebastian-software/impeccino) | Adaptation "
"and refinement of Impeccable design tooling, with contextual guidance and "
"reusable checks. |\n"
"\n"
"Core and Jasy were developed on our own initiative and later used extensively "
"at Zynga for our games' base library and build process. They brought together "
"reusable runtime infrastructure, dependency-aware builds, JavaScript "
"parsers/compilers, translation integration, assets, and developer tools.\n"
"\n"
"## Education and working context\n"
"\n"
"**1999–2001:** IT vocational qualification (Fachinformatiker) and "
"Fachabitur, Leo-Sympher-Berufskolleg, Minden. Early work included IT "
"administration and websites for small organizations.\n"
"\n"
"**Base:** Hirschberg/Bergstraße, Germany  \n"
"**Working languages:** German and English  \n"
"**Collaboration:** Remote work and occasional on-site collaboration  \n"
"**Contact:** "
"[s.werner@sebastian-software.de](mailto:s.werner@sebastian-software.de)"
msgstr ""
"# Sebastian Werner\n"
"\n"
"**Principal Technology Consultant · Ausführliches Projektprofil**\n"
"\n"
"Ich baue Frontend-Architekturen für neue Softwareprodukte auf und "
"modernisiere bestehende Plattformen. Internationalisierung, UI-Qualität, "
"Performance und Entwicklerwerkzeuge gehören regelmäßig zu meiner "
"Verantwortung. Meine Erfahrung umfasst Enterprise-Software, Banking, Energie, "
"Commerce, Telekommunikation und industrielle Anwendungen.\n"
"\n"
"## Projekterfahrung\n"
"\n"
"### 3Degrees · Meridian\n"
"\n"
"**November 2025–heute · Senior Principal Frontend Architect · Mandat für "
"einen US-Kunden**\n"
"\n"
"Für ein Energiemanagement-Produkt leite ich die Arbeit an visueller "
"Qualität, Internationalisierung und Frontend-Performance. Zu meinen "
"Beiträgen gehören Marketplace- und öffentliche Produktseiten, mobile "
"Layouts, SEO sowie getrennte Rendering-Pfade für öffentliche Seiten und "
"authentifizierte Portale.\n"
"\n"
"Ich führte die Lokalisierung ein und migrierte die Laufzeit von Lingui zu "
"Palamedes, einschließlich anfragebezogener Sprachbehandlung und der Grenzen "
"zwischen Übersetzungskatalogen für Server- und Client-Code. Die "
"Performance-Arbeit umfasst sprachabhängiges HTML- und Daten-Caching, weniger "
"Arbeit auf dem Client und progressives Streaming von Portfolioinformationen. "
"Das Team arbeitet vollständig auf Englisch und setzt KI-gestützte "
"Entwicklung umfassend ein.\n"
"\n"
"**Relevante Technologien:** TypeScript, React, Next.js, Palamedes, Lingui, "
"Vercel, Cloudflare, Supabase.\n"
"\n"
"### Regrello\n"
"\n"
"**Oktober 2024–September 2025 · Frontend Internationalization Lead · "
"Mandat für einen US-Kunden**\n"
"\n"
"Ich leitete die Internationalisierung einer bestehenden Enterprise-Anwendung. "
"Ich integrierte Lokalisierung in die Oberfläche und entwickelte Workflows "
"für Katalogextraktion, Kompilierung und LLM-gestützte Übersetzung. "
"Übersetzungsmetadaten und sprachabhängige Terminologie blieben dabei "
"erhalten.\n"
"\n"
"Im Rahmen einer gemeinsamen Initiative implementierte ich Oberflächen zur "
"Prüfung übersetzter Nutzerinhalte. Dazu gehörten Rich Text, "
"Erwähnungs-Platzhalter, berechtigungsabhängige Bearbeitung und asynchrone "
"Zustände.\n"
"\n"
"Ich migrierte außerdem den Frontend-Workspace von NX zu Turborepo, führte "
"striktes typbewusstes Linting ein und automatisierte die Migration von "
"GraphQL-Enums zu Union-Typen. Ich trennte Abhängigkeiten der "
"Komponentenentwicklung von der Hauptanwendung und ergänzte gezielte UI- und "
"End-to-End-Tests.\n"
"\n"
"**Relevante Technologien:** TypeScript, React, GraphQL, Lingui, Vite, "
"Turborepo, Storybook, Playwright.\n"
"\n"
"### EnBW · Kundenportale und Support-Arbeitsplatz\n"
"\n"
"**Juni 2022–Februar 2024 · Frontend Expert / React Architect**\n"
"\n"
"Ich arbeitete an Frontend-Architektur und Umsetzung für Self-Service- und "
"Support-Anwendungen. Die White-Label-Plattform unterstützte "
"mandantenspezifische Funktionen, Inhalte, Kommunikationsoptionen und "
"Gestaltung. Kundenabläufe umfassten Verträge, Rechnungen, Zählerstände, "
"Tarifwechsel und Umzüge.\n"
"\n"
"Ich entwickelte den PNPM-/Turborepo-Workspace, gemeinsame Theme- und "
"Konfigurationspakete, Storybook-Grundlagen, typisierte API-Integration und "
"wiederverwendbare Funktionen für den Datenzugriff. Ich dokumentierte, wie "
"sich Routing und Datenintegration von wiederverwendbaren, API-unabhängigen "
"Darstellungslayouts trennen lassen. Die Architektur nutzte "
"Headless-UI-Primitiven und typisierte Style-/Asset-Themes.\n"
"\n"
"**Relevante Technologien:** React, TypeScript, PNPM, Turborepo, Vite, "
"Storybook, Radix, VanillaExtract, SWR, REST, GraphQL.\n"
"\n"
"### Azeti · Industrielle Monitoring-Plattform\n"
"\n"
"**März–Mai 2022 · Senior React Developer**\n"
"\n"
"Ich unterstützte die Entwicklung eines industriellen Monitoring-Produkts mit "
"White-Label-Frontend. Meine Arbeit umfasste das NX-Monorepo, "
"Internationalisierung, Theming-Optionen und Anwendungskomponenten.\n"
"\n"
