msgid ""
"# Sebastian Werner\n"
"\n"
"**Principal Technology Consultant · Frontend Architecture, UI Quality & "
"Developer Experience**\n"
"\n"
"I help software teams and large organizations build new frontend platforms. I "
"make early architecture decisions and implement them with the team, drawing on"
" years of work with UI frameworks, internationalization, and developer "
"tooling. I also modernize existing frontends.\n"
"\n"
"I led development of the qooxdoo JavaScript UI framework at 1&1 and worked on "
"Deutsche Telekom's Unify framework and early Tolino browser software. Core and"
" Jasy were developed on our own initiative and used extensively at Zynga for "
"our games' base library and build process. Today, my infrastructure work also "
"includes Rust engines with TypeScript/Node.js interfaces.\n"
"\n"
"## Selected experience\n"
"\n"
"**Regrello — internationalization for an established enterprise platform**  "
"\n"
"I led the internationalization of a substantial enterprise application, "
"bringing translation into its UI and development workflow. This combined "
"Lingui localization, catalog tooling, and LLM-assisted translation. I also "
"contributed review interfaces for translated user content and modernized the "
"frontend workspace, linting, and component-development setup.\n"
"\n"
"**3Degrees — product UI, internationalization, and rendering performance**  "
"\n"
"I lead work on visual quality, internationalization, and frontend performance "
"for this US-based energy-management product. I introduced application "
"localization, migrated Lingui to Palamedes, and worked on public marketplace "
"pages, mobile layouts, SEO, caching, and streaming. The team works entirely in"
" English and uses AI-supported development extensively.\n"
"\n"
"**Otto Group — architecture for multilingual, multi-brand commerce**  \n"
"At Witt, I introduced GraphQL orchestration across backend services so the "
"shop frontend could use a consistent API. My work covered server rendering, "
"code splitting, build tooling, and internationalization for Eastern Europe. At"
" empiriecom, I contributed GraphQL and component-library development and "
"helped clarify implementation questions.\n"
"\n"
"**Deutsche Bank / DWS — frontend architecture for banking and investments**"
"  \n"
"For corporate banking and a robo-advisor investment platform, I contributed "
"frontend architecture, technology decisions, and interactive financial "
"visualizations. I worked with specialist and distributed teams within formal "
"approval and release processes.\n"
"\n"
"**Huawei / Deutsche Telekom and Zynga — performance for TV and game "
"interfaces**  \n"
"At EntertainTV, I implemented animations, layouts, and interaction on limited "
"set-top-box hardware. At Zynga, I worked on HTML5 game infrastructure, "
"scrolling, and developer tooling in a large JavaScript environment. Both "
"required detailed work on runtime behavior and UI performance.\n"
"\n"
"**EnBW — a shared frontend foundation for white-label portals**  \n"
"I built shared monorepo, theme, component, and typed API foundations for "
"customer portals and a support workbench. The platform supported "
"tenant-specific features, content, and visual identity. I documented how to "
"separate data integration from reusable UI components.\n"
"\n"
"## Open-source development\n"
"\n"
"I build and maintain open-source tools to give back to the developer "
"community. These projects make work on architecture, internationalization, and"
" performance available for others to use and build on:\n"
"\n"
"- [Palamedes](https://github.com/sebastian-software/palamedes) and "
"[Ferrocat](https://github.com/sebastian-software/ferrocat): application "
"internationalization, translation catalogs, Rust engines, and typed Node.js "
"integration.\n"
"- [Ferroni](https://github.com/sebastian-software/ferroni) and "
"[Ferriki](https://github.com/sebastian-software/ferriki): Rust ports, "
"compatibility work, native JavaScript interfaces, and performance "
"engineering.\n"
"- [Ardo](https://github.com/sebastian-software/ardo), [Effective "
"Agent](https://github.com/sebastian-software/effective-agent), and [Effective "
"Icon](https://github.com/sebastian-software/effective-icon): documentation, "
"engineering guidance, and build-time UI tooling.\n"
"\n"
"## How I work\n"
"\n"
"I especially enjoy greenfield work: helping a team establish the architecture "
"and tooling for a new product. My web-design background shapes how I judge "
"layout, motion, and interaction. I share knowledge through reviews, "
"documentation, and mentoring. I contribute through long-term implementation "
"engagements, architecture reviews, and workshops.\n"
"\n"
"**Based in:** Hirschberg/Bergstraße, Germany · Remote collaboration and "
"occasional on-site work  \n"
"**Working languages:** German and English  \n"
"**Contact:** "
"[s.werner@sebastian-software.de](mailto:s.werner@sebastian-software.de)"
